From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build_scripts: skip the designer plugin copy when it was
 not built

Upstream-Status: To upstream [no Gerrit account to submit to Qt's code review]

prepare_standalone_package_linux() unconditionally copies
{install_dir}/plugins/designer into the wheel's Qt/plugins/designer,
with no existence guard (unlike every other optional copydir() call in
this same function, which pass force=False). On this build the PySide
Designer custom-widget plugin component isn't produced -- Rocky 10's
qt6-qt*-devel packages carry Designer's headers/libs but not its
runtime application pieces, same gap --no-qt-tools already works
around for the bundled assistant/designer/linguist executables -- so
plugins/designer never exists under install/, and the build failed
with:

  setup.py/prepare_packages:  [Errno 2] No such file or directory:
  '.../install/plugins/designer'

Pass force=False, same as the adjacent qt_translations_dir and
shiboken6 docs/html copies in this file, so a missing optional
component is skipped (logged) instead of aborting the build. The
Designer plugin is only consumed by the standalone Designer *app* to
load custom PySide widgets, not by `import PySide6.QtDesigner` itself.

diff --git a/build_scripts/platforms/linux.py b/build_scripts/platforms/linux.py
index 32ad9da..464a8ca 100644
--- a/build_scripts/platforms/linux.py
+++ b/build_scripts/platforms/linux.py
@@ -101,6 +101,7 @@ def prepare_standalone_package_linux(pyside_build, _vars, cross_build=False, is
                     plugins_target / "designer",
                     _filter=["*.so"],
                     recursive=False,
+                    force=False,
                     _vars=_vars)

         copied_plugins = pyside_build.get_shared_libraries_in_path_recursively(
--
